> The story at the top of this page is a rewrite of the longer account, which is kept under "For those who want to check". Two more fresh copies of the model read this rewrite: one read the story alone, as a stranger would, for plainness, and checked no facts; the other checked the story, its two pictures and the new section on the hours against the working notes, their saved results and the papers, and only compared the rest of the longer account with the earlier page. The second ran none of the computations again and made no search for other publications, and its changes have not been read again. After those readings I folded the section "Why 205 BC" behind its heading, to shorten the page, and moved one sentence (on the marks that can still be read) down a paragraph, where the pasting had left it between a statement and its answer; no word of either was changed. On 27 November the sentence beginning "In short" was added to the first paragraph, and a link to the full-size picture under each picture in the open text; a fresh copy read the sentence against this page.
> 
