> In the section on the eclipse dial the sentence on which months lose their eclipses first was made plainer, and the figures for eclipses in months without a mark and the count without the faint eclipses were taken out of the open text (all of that is in the longer account). The words "and counted strictly the dial did less well" were added. The sentence on the eclipse of 3 March 2026 was brought up from the longer account. The sentence on the last marked months now says "marked for the Moon" and "marked for the Sun", and the second published list of marks, which had a clause of its own higher up, is now a sentence in brackets beside it that says what that list changes; the names of its authors are in the longer account.
